{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CevMDpaUp1qhAReYachU4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Repository findings:**\n- `Order.kt:11-16` — Order data class has no status field yet\n- `OrderController.kt:16-46` — Has POST create, GET getById, GET list but no cancel endpoint\n- `OrderRepository.kt:10-27` — In-memory store with save, findById, existsById, findAll\n- `Shipment.kt:23-27` — ShipmentStatus enum exists with CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED values\n- `ShipmentRepository.kt:10-27` — In-memory store with same pattern as OrderRepository\n- `ShipmentController.kt:26-44` — Create endpoint doesn't check order status\n- `ApiError.kt:31-37` — ErrorCode enum is the single source of error codes\n- `GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:14-29` — Centralized handler for all ApiExceptions\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n- In-memory ConcurrentHashMap repositories, no JPA\n- Controllers throw ApiException subclasses directly (ConflictException, ResourceNotFoundException)\n- ErrorCode enum is maintained in one place and exhaustive\n- HTTP status and error code both come from the exception, enforced by GlobalExceptionHandler\n- Tests verify both HTTP status and `$.error.code` in the body\n- Status enums already exist for Shipment; same pattern needed for Order\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. **Order.kt** — Add `OrderStatus` enum and `status` field (required for the feature)\n2. **OrderController.kt** — Add `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint (required for the feature)\n3. **OrderRepository.kt** — Add `findByOrderId` method to find shipments by order (required to cancel them)\n4. **ShipmentRepository.kt** — Add `findByOrderId` method for the same reason\n5. **ShipmentController.kt** — Check order status before creating shipment (required for rejection of shipments to cancelled orders)\n6. **ApiError.kt** — Add error codes for order-cancelled and order-has-confirmed-shipment scenarios (required for 409 responses)\n7. **OrderControllerTest.kt** — Add tests for all cancel cases (required for acceptance criteria 3, 4, 5)\n\n**Risks:**\n- Adding a status field to Order makes it a breaking model change if not handled carefully in tests\n- Cancelling shipments must be atomic — if any shipment is CONFIRMED, the entire cancel fails with no changes\n- Shipment creation needs to know the order's status, creating a dependency between features\n\n**Open questions:** None — all cases the ticket names are defined.\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed changes:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** — Add `OrderStatus` enum (ACTIVE, CANCELLED) and add a `status: OrderStatus = OrderStatus.ACTIVE` field to the Order data class. New orders default to ACTIVE.\n\n2. **OrderController.kt** — Add a `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint that:\n   - Throws `ResourceNotFoundException` with `ORDER_NOT_FOUND` if order doesn't exist\n   - If order is already CANCELLED, returns it with 200 OK (idempotent)\n   - If any shipment is CONFIRMED, throws `ConflictException` with `ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT` and changes nothing\n   - Otherwise, sets order status to CANCELLED, cancels all CREATED shipments of that order, persists changes, returns the order with 200 OK\n\n3. **OrderRepository.kt** — Add `findAll()` method to get all shipments (only necessary if ShipmentRepository doesn't have findByOrderId). Actually, need to think about this — the OrderController will need to get shipments for an order. ShipmentRepository needs a `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` method.\n\n4. **ShipmentRepository.kt** — Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` to return all shipments for a given order ID.\n\n5. **ShipmentController.kt** — In the create endpoint, after checking shipment doesn't already exist, also check that the order exists and is not CANCELLED. If order is CANCELLED, throw `ConflictException` with `ORDER_CANCELLED` code.\n\n6. **ApiError.kt** — Add two error codes:\n   - `ORDER_CANCELLED` — for when trying to create a shipment for a cancelled order\n   - `ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT` — for when trying to cancel an order with a confirmed shipment\n\n7. **OrderControllerTest.kt** — Add tests for:\n   - Cancelling an active order (moves to CANCELLED, cancels CREATED shipments)\n   - Cancelling an already-cancelled order (succeeds, changes nothing, returns order)\n   - Cancelling an order with a CONFIRMED shipment (returns 409, nothing changes)\n   - Cancelling a non-existent order (returns 404)\n\n**Alternative rejected:**\n- Could use a service layer between controller and repository, but the existing codebase has controllers calling repositories directly with no service layer, so staying consistent with that pattern\n- Could have shipment repository methods private and expose them only through a service, but that adds unnecessary indirection given the in-memory nature and lack of transactions\n- Could return 200 with no body for a failed cancel, but HTTP semantics say 409 is the right code for \"conflict with current state\"\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n1. **Cancel active order**: POST /orders/O-1/cancel where O-1 exists and is ACTIVE\n   - Controller loads order from repository\n   - Controller checks order exists (throw 404 if not)\n   - Controller gets all shipments for that order\n   - Controller checks if any is CONFIRMED (throw 409 with ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT if so)\n   - Controller sets order status to CANCELLED\n   - Controller sets all CREATED shipments to CANCELLED\n   - Controller saves order and all shipments\n   - Returns 200 with order in body\n\n2. **Cancel already-cancelled order**: POST /orders/O-1/cancel where O-1 is CANCELLED\n   - Controller loads order\n   - Controller checks order exists (throw 404 if not)\n   - Controller sees status is CANCELLED\n   - Returns 200 with order in body (idempotent, no changes)\n\n3. **Cancel order with CONFIRMED shipment**: POST /orders/O-1/cancel where O-1 is ACTIVE and has a CONFIRMED shipment\n   - Controller loads order\n   - Controller checks order exists (throw 404 if not)\n   - Controller gets all shipments for that order\n   - Controller finds a CONFIRMED shipment\n   - Throws ConflictException with ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT\n   - Nothing is changed\n   - Returns 409 with error body\n\n4. **Create shipment for cancelled order**: POST /shipments with orderId=O-1 where O-1 is CANCELLED\n   - Controller checks shipment doesn't already exist (throw 409 if it does)\n   - Controller loads order from repository\n   - If order is CANCELLED, throw ConflictException with ORDER_CANCELLED\n   - Otherwise proceed with creation\n\n5. **Cancel non-existent order**: POST /orders/O-999/cancel where O-999 doesn't exist\n   - Controller tries to load order\n   - Order is null\n   - Throws ResourceNotFoundException with ORDER_NOT_FOUND\n   - Returns 404 with error body\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\nNew tests in OrderControllerTest:\n- `cancelsAnActiveOrder` — Create order, get it, cancel it, verify status is CANCELLED, verify response is 200 with order in body\n- `cancellingAlreadyCancelledOrderSucceeds` — Create order, cancel it, cancel it again, verify 200 and order is still CANCELLED (idempotent)\n- `cancelOrderWithConfirmedShipmentFails` — Create order, create shipment in CONFIRMED state (write directly to repo), try to cancel, verify 409 with ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT, verify order still ACTIVE in repo\n- `cancelNonExistentOrderFails` — Try to cancel order that doesn't exist, verify 404 with ORDER_NOT_FOUND\n- May need to add tests to verify CREATED shipments are cancelled when order is cancelled\n\nAdditional test in ShipmentControllerTest:\n- `rejectsCreatingShipmentForCancelledOrder` — Create order, cancel it, try to create shipment, verify 409 with ORDER_CANCELLED\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":404,"cache_read_input_tokens":20794,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":404},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1f8d197c-81f9-4dc1-9185-e15a34efe528","uuid":"e9a2ff4c-fde4-419d-b3b4-346d7517c662","timestamp":"2026-09-10T19:58:06.265Z","request_id":"req_011CevMDoyWppCYWiQbSVJYV"}
