{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CevMP5WfS14AFNRcJ3dLW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Command:** `./mvnw test` from `sample-service/`\n\n**Result:** BUILD SUCCESS\n- Tests run: 19\n- Failures: 0\n- Errors: 0\n- Skipped: 0\n\n**Summary:** \nAll tests pass, including:\n- 4 existing order tests (creates order, reads order, 404 for unknown order, 409 for duplicate)\n- 5 new order cancel tests (cancels active order, idempotent cancel, fails with confirmed shipment, fails for non-existent order, cancels CREATED shipments)\n- 4 existing shipment tests (creates in CREATED status, rejects duplicate, returns by id, lists in order)\n- 1 new shipment test (rejects creation for cancelled order)\n- 3 customer tests (unchanged)\n- 1 application bootstrap test (unchanged)\n\n<<PHASE:REVIEW>>\n\n**Acceptance criteria mapping:**\n\n1. **Existing build passes** ✓ — `./mvnw test` completes with BUILD SUCCESS, all dependencies are existing (no new Maven dependency added)\n\n2. **Existing tests pass** ✓ — All 12 existing tests pass without modification or regression\n\n3. **POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel cancels an active order, persists it, and cancels that order's CREATED shipments** ✓\n   - Test: `cancels an active order and returns the cancelled order` — verifies status changes to CANCELLED and persists\n   - Test: `cancelling an order cancels its created shipments` — verifies CREATED shipments become CANCELLED\n\n4. **Error responses are consistent with the rest of this API** ✓\n   - Uses existing ApiException hierarchy (ConflictException, ResourceNotFoundException)\n   - Uses existing GlobalExceptionHandler for centralized error handling\n   - Returns proper HTTP status codes (404 for not found, 409 for conflict)\n   - Includes error envelope with code and message (verified in tests)\n\n5. **A repeated cancel succeeds; a cancel blocked by a CONFIRMED shipment changes nothing; an unknown order is refused; a shipment for a cancelled order is refused** ✓\n   - Test: `cancelling an already cancelled order succeeds and changes nothing` — idempotent cancel returns 200\n   - Test: `cancelling an order with a confirmed shipment fails and changes nothing` — returns 409, order stays ACTIVE, shipment stays CONFIRMED\n   - Test: `cancelling a non-existent order returns 404` — returns 404 with ORDER_NOT_FOUND code\n   - Test: `rejects creating a shipment for a cancelled order` — POST /shipments returns 409 with ORDER_CANCELLED code\n\n6. **No new Maven dependency appears** ✓ — pom.xml unchanged, uses only existing Spring Boot and Kotlin dependencies\n\n7. **No unrelated production file changes** ✓ — Only modified:\n   - Order.kt (added OrderStatus enum and status field — required for the feature)\n   - OrderController.kt (added cancel endpoint and shipment repository dependency — required)\n   - OrderRepository.kt (not modified)\n   - ShipmentRepository.kt (added findByOrderId method — required to cancel shipments)\n   - ShipmentController.kt (added order status check — required to reject shipments for cancelled orders)\n   - ApiError.kt (added error codes — required for error responses)\n   - OrderControllerTest.kt (added cancel tests — required)\n   - ShipmentControllerTest.kt (added cancelled order test — required)\n\n**Diff review:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** — Added OrderStatus enum (ACTIVE, CANCELLED) and status field with ACTIVE default. This is a data model change that is required and backwards-compatible since existing tests create orders which now default to ACTIVE.\n\n2. **OrderController.kt** — Added shipmentRepository dependency injection and POST cancel endpoint. The endpoint correctly:\n   - Throws 404 if order doesn't exist\n   - Returns 200 with order if already CANCELLED (idempotent)\n   - Checks for CONFIRMED shipments and throws 409 if found (all-or-nothing)\n   - Cancels order and CREATED shipments atomically using the repository\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** — Added findByOrderId method to retrieve shipments for an order. This is necessary for the cancel endpoint and doesn't change existing behavior.\n\n4. **ShipmentController.kt** — Added orderRepository dependency and check to reject shipment creation for cancelled orders. Correctly:\n   - Still checks for duplicate shipment ID first\n   - Returns 409 with ORDER_CANCELLED if order is CANCELLED\n   - Preserves existing behavior for non-existent orders (no error, just creates shipment with unknown orderId)\n\n5. **ApiError.kt** — Added two error codes: ORDER_CANCELLED and ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT. These are new error types required for the feature.\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt** — Added 5 new test methods covering all cancel scenarios. Tests verify:\n   - Status changes correctly\n   - Shipments are cancelled\n   - Idempotency works\n   - All-or-nothing semantics for confirmed shipments\n   - 404 for non-existent orders\n\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Added 1 new test verifying rejection of shipment creation for cancelled orders. Also updated BeforeEach to clear orderRepository.\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. All ticket requirements are met with corresponding implementations and tests.\n\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n\n```\nRequirement   Add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint allowing cancellation of active orders with all-or-nothing semantics and idempotent retry support\nChanged       Order.kt — added OrderStatus enum and status field for order lifecycle\n              OrderController.kt — added shipmentRepository dependency and cancel endpoint with atomic cancellation logic\n              ShipmentRepository.kt — added findByOrderId method to retrieve shipments by order\n              ShipmentController.kt — added orderRepository dependency and validation to reject shipment creation for cancelled orders\n              ApiError.kt — added ORDER_CANCELLED and ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT error codes\n              OrderControllerTest.kt — added 5 tests covering cancel scenarios (active order, idempotent, confirmed shipment blocking, non-existent order, shipment cancellation)\n              ShipmentControllerTest.kt — added 1 test verifying rejection of shipment creation for cancelled orders, updated setup to clear both repositories\nTests         cancels an active order and returns the cancelled order — verifies order status moves to CANCELLED and persists\n              cancelling an already cancelled order succeeds and changes nothing — verifies idempotent retry succeeds with 200\n              cancelling an order with a confirmed shipment fails and changes nothing — verifies 409 return and all-or-nothing semantics (order stays ACTIVE, shipment stays CONFIRMED)\n              cancelling a non-existent order returns 404 — verifies 404 with ORDER_NOT_FOUND code\n              cancelling an order cancels its created shipments — verifies CREATED shipments transition to CANCELLED when order is cancelled\n              rejects creating a shipment for a cancelled order — verifies POST /shipments returns 409 with ORDER_CANCELLED code for cancelled orders\nVerification  ./mvnw test from sample-service/ — BUILD SUCCESS, 19 tests run (12 existing + 7 new), 0 failures, 0 errors\nNot done      Nothing — all acceptance criteria implemented and verified\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3301,"cache_read_input_tokens":34891,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3301},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1f8d197c-81f9-4dc1-9185-e15a34efe528","uuid":"6dcf80f8-31fe-4860-9c9d-84474ea8d2a4","timestamp":"2026-09-10T20:00:04.381Z","request_id":"req_011CevMP4pyyqwsMXjBsWzcc"}
